                                        "sense_id": "eba1b598-e414-39ff-b966-8d75deba1d78",
                                        "entry_id": "0be0297e-34ed-3a1d-8994-cd4a4d9d80f2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a prodigious manner; astonishingly, enormously, impressively, wonderfully."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7568913e-06ca-430a-ab67-85b17661b0d1",
                                                "sense_id": "eba1b598-e414-39ff-b966-8d75deba1d78",
                                                "text": "[T]he Mercers encreaſing prodigiouſly vvent back into the City; there like Bees unhiv'd they hover about a vvhile, not knovving vvhere to fix; but at laſt, as if they vvould come back to the old Hive in Pater-noſter Rovv, but could not be admitted, the ſvvarm ſettled on Lu[d]gate-hill."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dff59a76-1a61-4c78-8a76-72404dfd660f",
                                                "sense_id": "eba1b598-e414-39ff-b966-8d75deba1d78",
                                                "text": "The Dashwoods were so prodigiously delighted with the Middletons, that, though not much in the habit of giving any thing, they determined to give them—a dinner; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bef49b1e-7d6c-4e08-92f7-aedbfe553dee",
                                                "sense_id": "eba1b598-e414-39ff-b966-8d75deba1d78",
                                                "text": "Pendennis the elder, who like a real man of the world had a proper and constant dread of the opinion of his neighbour, was prodigiously annoyed by the absurd little tempest which was blowing in Chatteris, and tossing about Master Pen’s reputation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
